    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17926" textLabel="MONOMER-17926" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q7XHW5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="100.0" centerY="798.4712524414062" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, dreher">CYP714B1 is a member of the cytochrome P450 family of enzymes that catalyzes the formation of |FRAME: CPD-659 GA53| (gibberellin A53) from |FRAME: CPD1F-95 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;| in the first committed step of the |FRAME: PWY-5035 early C13 hydroxylation gibberellin biosynthesis pathway| |CITS: [23319637]|. When this recombinant His-tagged protein is tested against several other potential gibberellins and gibberellin precursors, including |FRAME: CPD1F-132 ent-kaurenoic acid|, |FRAME: CPD1F-134 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;|, and |FRAME: CPD1F-137 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;|, using the same yeast microsomal fraction assay CYP714B1 shows no activity |CITS: [23319637]|. A closely related enzyme, CYP714B2, catalyzes the same reaction in rice and a &lt;i&gt;cyp714b1 cyb714b2&lt;/i&gt; double mutant has reduced levels of several GA compounds found downstream of |FRAME: CPD1F-95 GA12| in the |FRAME: PWY-5035 early C13 hydroxylation gibberellin biosynthesis pathway|, including |FRAME: CPD-695 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;53&lt;/sub&gt;| and the bioactive |FRAME: CPD1F-139 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;|. It also has increased levels of the compounds produced in an alternative |FRAME: PWY-5070 non-C13 hydroxylation pathway|, including |FRAME: CPD1F-134 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;| and |FRAME: CPD1F-137 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;|. However, some 13-hydroxylated GAs can be detected in this double mutant, suggesting that additional enzymes might also catalyze gibberellin C13 oxidation in rice. This is further supported by the observation of soluble gibberellin 13-oxidase activity in other plant species |CITS: 16664991| while CYP714B1 is expected to be a membrane-bound protein |CITS: [23319637]|. In addition, there is some evidence of multifunctional GA-metabolizing enzymes that have weak C13-oxidase activity, such as |FRAME: MONOMER-11644 TaGA3ox2| in wheat |CITS: [16160850]|. CYP714B1 transcript levels increase following treatment with the bioactive GAs |FRAME: CPD1F-137 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;| and |FRAME: GIBBERELLIN gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;| |CITS: [23319637]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-17926" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os07t0681300-00" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS00086" />
